      "markdown": "### Executive Order No. 13166: Improving Access to Services for Persons with Limited English Proficiency (LEP)\n\nAugust 11, 2000: President Bill Clinton issued the Executive Order 13166.\n\nDesigned to improve access to federally conducted and federally assisted programs/activities for LEP persons\n\nFederal agencies were asked to develop and implement a system to provide LEP persons access to services.\n\nEach federal agency was asked to prepare a plan to improve access to LEP persons, and submit plans to the U.S. Department of Justice.\n\nExecutive Order charged the Department of Justice with the responsibility of providing LEP guidance to federal agencies.",
